// THE AMDUAT ("Book of what is in the Underworld"; Budge's "Book Am-Tuat"), in
// Budge's English from The Egyptian Heaven and Hell, vol. I (1905), hour by
// hour, with the Short Form ("Summary") of vol. II beside it.
//
// The text comes from amduat-text.ts, generated by
// scripts/texts/budge-underworld.py. Each of the twelve hours is a passage
// with no text of its own; beneath it Budge's chapter is cut where he turns
// from the scene's opening to its middle, upper and lower registers. The
// twelve hours of the Short Form sit under a separate 'version' passage and
// are not counted as units. Budge's hieroglyphs and transliteration are left
// out. Hornung's edition and the modern English translations (Abt & Hornung,
// Warburton, the Darnells) are in copyright and are cited, never quoted.
//
// Nothing is marked verified, and the twelve has not been checked against
// Hornung's edition (inventoryVerified stays false).

